# Local rollback/backup artifacts (post-content dumps, DB/option snapshots,
# pre-deploy file copies) must never enter public git history - keep them
# outside the repo (see docs/DOCUMENTATION_GOVERNANCE.md's public/private
# classification). Record only the rollback location class + timestamp in
# release/worklog docs, never the content itself.
/backups/

# Unsanitized internal operational records (Mailchimp campaign IDs, coupon
# codes, internal automation URLs, test-contact identifiers). Public docs
# under docs/ must use descriptive placeholders only - see
# docs-private/MAILCHIMP_INTERNAL_REFERENCE.md for the real values.
/docs-private/

# Private Business OS / strategy working copies and scratch research.
# These mirror the private Google Drive knowledge base (decision registers,
# competitor intelligence, conversion audits) and contain live coupon codes.
# Never commit them - the repo is public. See CLAUDE.md's CSO rule.
/.codex-business-os-update/
/.codex-business-os-before-growth-update/
/tmp/

# Local operational configuration (per-machine permission grants and
# session settings). Never commit - it is machine-specific, not project
# state. Also ignored machine-wide, but pinned here so the protection
# travels with the repository.
/.claude/settings.local.json
